{
  "name": "419. Sora 2 on Azure: undeliverable fields refused, extra fields carried, content blocks classified, task object, no cancel, named key (azure sora 2)",
  "description": "Pins contract C3, C4, C5, C6, C7, C9 and C12 for Sora 2 on Azure (TXE-6532). Local fixture regression, no live provider calls: start tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs, start an isolated gateway on tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json and run with providerErrorFixture=1; every case is skipped otherwise. The azure provider has two keys, azure-sora-a and azure-sora-b, each on its own resource path of the fixture, so the counters in the last row prove which resource and key each call used. Rows 2 and 7 to 8 are refused before any upstream call. Row 9 carries x-bf-passthrough-extra-params. Row 15 is the cancel route; the last row asserts no DELETE reached Azure.",
